{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Hold a public inquiry into securitised mortgages and bank guarantee practices",
        "additional_details": "Many borrowers and guarantors have reported being unable to establish who legally owns their debt or to obtain clear records when facilities were sold on or securitised. We believe this raises serious questions of consumer protection; financial conduct and access to justice that warrant independent public scrutiny as non-novated securitised mortgages fail the Regulated Mortgage Contract (RMC) test.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to launch a public inquiry into the sale, securitisation and enforcement of mortgage backed securities and bank guarantees by UK banks over the past 3 decades including the transparency of non-novated loan ownership transfers and the adequacy of regulatory oversight by FCA",
